# Planted-bug tests behind the README's Verification table. Everything below the "command:" line
# is that command's complete output (make's echo of the recipe, with the virtualenv path shortened
# to <venv python>; the report; then the wall time from /usr/bin/time -p). These notes were
# written after the run.
#
# How the table's figures come out of the rows below:
# - Accuracy column: 11.33%, 81.00%, 98.33%, 98.33% (the README rounds to one decimal).
# - 03_no_round: "hidden 0/300" means the hidden activations differ from the golden model on all
#   300 images; "digit 299/300" means the predicted digit differs on 1 of the 300 (image 247).
#   Its accuracy, 295/300 = 98.33%, is the same as the correct design's.
# - 04_argmax_ge passes: the data facts below show no image with two equal top logits, in the
#   first 300 or in all 10,000 (the closest gap is 1), so the mutated compare never decides.
# - 02_acc16's "layer-2 0/300" is partly the testbench comparing a 10 x 16-bit accumulator bus
#   with 10 x 24-bit expected values; its hidden and digit columns are the meaningful ones.
#
################################################################
# command: make mutants PYTHON=<venv python>   (run from the repo root, Apple M2, macOS 15.1)
PYTHON=<venv python> bash mutants/run_mutants.sh > sim/mutants.log; \
	status=$?; cat sim/mutants.log; exit $status
# Planted-bug tests: bash mutants/run_mutants.sh
